{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-26352","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30573","text":"RRABBIT"}]},{"id":"blk-26353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30574","text":"The road as a windowing system — half of "},{"id":"spn-30575","marks":["bold"],"text":"T&R (Travel & RRABBIT)"},{"id":"spn-30576","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30577","marks":["bold"],"text":"Travel and RRABBIT are two personalities, not two layers."},{"id":"spn-30578","text":" Travel wants to navigate: the road, the camera, the flight into a window, the districts. RRABBIT wants to "},{"id":"spn-30579","marks":["italic"],"text":"be"},{"id":"spn-30580","text":" the windows — the sign standing on the road, the surface that flattens to 1:1 under you, the rect that decides a click is yours. One likes going; the other likes being gone to."}]},{"id":"blk-26355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30581","text":"This repo is a fork of "},{"id":"spn-30582","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../RAVIO"}],"text":"RAVIO"},{"id":"spn-30583","text":"'s world, re-missioned from "},{"id":"spn-30584","marks":["italic"],"text":"rendering a build harness"},{"id":"spn-30585","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-30586","marks":["italic"],"text":"managing an operating system's windows"},{"id":"spn-30587","text":", and it holds both of them — as two modules rather than one file:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-26357","spans":[{"id":"spn-30588","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-26358","spans":[{"id":"spn-30589","text":"who"}]},{"id":"blk-26359","spans":[{"id":"spn-30590","text":"what is in it"}]}],"id":"blk-26356","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-26360","spans":[{"id":"spn-30591","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/travel.js"}],"text":"`m2/travel.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26361","spans":[{"id":"spn-30592","text":"Travel"}]},{"id":"blk-26362","spans":[{"id":"spn-30593","text":"poses, districts, overview, the flatten, the flight, input routing"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26363","spans":[{"id":"spn-30594","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/rrabbit.js"}],"text":"`m2/rrabbit.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26364","spans":[{"id":"spn-30595","text":"RRABBIT"}]},{"id":"blk-26365","spans":[{"id":"spn-30596","text":"texture adoption, signs, popups, the ledger rect"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26366","spans":[{"id":"spn-30597","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/world.js"}],"text":"`m2/world.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26367","spans":[{"id":"spn-30598","text":"neither"}]},{"id":"blk-26368","spans":[{"id":"spn-30599","text":"the stage: scene handles, the "},{"id":"spn-30600","marks":["code"],"text":"signs"},{"id":"spn-30601","text":" ledger, the numbers the HUD reads"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26369","spans":[{"id":"spn-30602","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/shell.js"}],"text":"`m2/shell.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26370","spans":[{"id":"spn-30603","text":"the wiring"}]},{"id":"blk-26371","spans":[{"id":"spn-30604","text":"builds the world, drives the frame, owns the diagnostics"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-26372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30605","text":"They say very little to each other. Travel reads two things and both come through the shared ledger rather than a call — which sign stands at an address, and what rect it owns in the flat output. RRABBIT calls Travel "},{"id":"spn-30606","marks":["bold"],"text":"once"},{"id":"spn-30607","text":": when a window dies while you are standing in it, it tells Travel to let go. That is the whole conversation, and it runs in one direction."}]},{"id":"blk-26373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30608","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/travel-and-rrabbit"}],"text":"travel-and-rrabbit"},{"id":"spn-30609","text":" is the distribution — it carries Travel's name and is not Travel either."}]},{"id":"blk-26374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30610","text":"Signs on the road are no longer journal rows. "},{"id":"spn-30611","marks":["bold"],"text":"They are the running applications."},{"id":"spn-30612","text":" The vacuum tubes are no longer lane ratings; they are CPU, RAM, swap, disk, net, temp and load. Districts are no longer amp workspaces; they are desktop workspaces. You drive past your windows, fly into one, and it flattens into a real, square, pixel-exact surface you can type into."}]},{"id":"blk-26375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30613","text":"It shows only windows launched into it. It does not replace your desktop."}]},{"id":"blk-26376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30614","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read [`docs/spec/README.md`](docs/spec/README.md) first"},{"id":"spn-30615","text":" — in particular §2, which records what does "},{"id":"spn-30616","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-30617","text":" work about the obvious integration and why."}]},{"id":"blk-26377","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30618","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-26378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30619","marks":["bold"],"text":"M0–M5 built, M0–M4 measured"},{"id":"spn-30620","text":" (2026-08-08), each with measurements rather than screenshots alone — spec §10–§12 and §14–§17. "},{"id":"spn-30621","marks":["bold"],"text":"Booted on T&R 2026-08-09."}]},{"id":"blk-26379","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26381","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30622","marks":["bold"],"text":"M0"},{"id":"spn-30623","text":" — the road occludes a live Wayland surface. This was the gate."}]}],"id":"blk-26380","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30624","marks":["bold"],"text":"M1"},{"id":"spn-30625","text":" — many windows ride the road as signs, one adopted GPU texture each,"}]}],"id":"blk-26382","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30626","text":"at stable milepost addresses. No Greenfield patch was needed after all (§11.1)."}]},{"id":"blk-26385","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30627","marks":["bold"],"text":"M2"},{"id":"spn-30628","text":" — flying into a sign arrives fronto-parallel at exactly 1:1, where it"}]}],"id":"blk-26386","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30629","text":"can be pointed at, typed into, and left with a chord no client can swallow."}]},{"id":"blk-26389","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30630","marks":["bold"],"text":"M3"},{"id":"spn-30631","text":" — seven tubes reading the real machine, and a rack that is not allowed"}]}],"id":"blk-26390","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26392","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30632","text":"to show a number it cannot explain."}]},{"id":"blk-26393","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30633","marks":["bold"],"text":"M4"},{"id":"spn-30634","text":" — three districts as workspaces, each a road of its own, and a ledger"}]}],"id":"blk-26394","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26396","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30635","text":"where every window has its own rect so input resolves by position (§15.2)."}]},{"id":"blk-26397","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30636","marks":["bold"],"text":"popups"},{"id":"spn-30637","text":" — §7's open problem, closed (§16). Also found that an "},{"id":"spn-30638","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"}]}],"id":"blk-26398","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26400","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30639","text":"cannot map at all in Greenfield rc1."}]},{"id":"blk-26401","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30640","marks":["bold"],"text":"M5"},{"id":"spn-30641","text":" — runs as a session: Python-only on the target, and Firefox runs the"}]}],"id":"blk-26402","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30642","text":"whole shell."}]},{"id":"blk-26405","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30643","marks":["bold"],"text":"BOOT"},{"id":"spn-30644","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-30645","marks":["bold"],"text":"runs on a T&R image"},{"id":"spn-30646","text":" (2026-08-09). Greeter to road on the"}]}],"id":"blk-26406","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26408","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30647","text":"distribution it is built for, in a 4 GB guest with no GPU. Six of seven tubes read the real FreeBSD machine; "},{"id":"spn-30648","marks":["code"],"text":"temp"},{"id":"spn-30649","text":" reports its own absence, because a VM has no "},{"id":"spn-30650","marks":["code"],"text":"dev.cpu.0.temperature"},{"id":"spn-30651","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30652","text":"Three things that only a real boot could have found, all now fixed:"}]},{"id":"blk-26410","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30653","marks":["bold"],"text":"`make.sh` could not carry the shell to the builder at all."},{"id":"spn-30654","text":" "},{"id":"spn-30655","marks":["code"],"text":"build-image.sh"}]}],"id":"blk-26411","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30656","text":"reads "},{"id":"spn-30657","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT_DIST"},{"id":"spn-30658","text":" as a path on the machine doing the build, and that machine is never the workstation — so there was no route from a built bundle to an image. It pushes "},{"id":"spn-30659","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-30660","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-30661","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.py"},{"id":"spn-30662","text":" now, and refuses a "},{"id":"spn-30663","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-30664","text":" older than its sources."}]},{"id":"blk-26414","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30665","marks":["bold"],"text":"The FreeBSD tube reader had never executed."},{"id":"spn-30666","text":" "},{"id":"spn-30667","marks":["code"],"text":"net"},{"id":"spn-30668","text":" raised "},{"id":"spn-30669","marks":["code"],"text":"TypeError"},{"id":"spn-30670","text":" on a"}]}],"id":"blk-26415","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30671","marks":["code"],"text":"None"},{"id":"spn-30672","text":" peak the first time it ran. Fixed by giving it the same prior-peak protocol "},{"id":"spn-30673","marks":["code"],"text":"LinuxReader"},{"id":"spn-30674","text":" already had — patching only the crash would have re-introduced the bug that note describes, where the first byte pins the gauge at 100%."}]},{"id":"blk-26418","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30675","marks":["bold"],"text":"The greeter preselected RRABBIT, and could not select anything else."},{"id":"spn-30676","text":" Two"}]}],"id":"blk-26419","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26421","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30677","marks":["code"],"text":".desktop"},{"id":"spn-30678","text":" entries, picked by sort order, and "},{"id":"spn-30679","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit"},{"id":"spn-30680","text":" sorts before "},{"id":"spn-30681","marks":["code"],"text":"tandr"},{"id":"spn-30682","text":" — so a fresh image logged into the 3D shell, which is precisely what "},{"id":"spn-30683","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit-session"},{"id":"spn-30684","text":" says must never happen. The session label was blank as well: it asked SDDM's "},{"id":"spn-30685","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionModel"},{"id":"spn-30686","text":" for "},{"id":"spn-30687","marks":["code"],"text":"Qt.DisplayRole"},{"id":"spn-30688","text":", which that model does not publish. T&R now seeds the default and the greeter takes "},{"id":"spn-30689","marks":["bold"],"text":"F2"},{"id":"spn-30690","text":" to change it."}]},{"id":"blk-26422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30691","marks":["bold"],"text":"Native applications work"},{"id":"spn-30692","text":" (§18). A real "},{"id":"spn-30693","marks":["code"],"text":"xterm"},{"id":"spn-30694","text":" runs on the road — X11 → XWayland → nested compositor → h264 → browser → GPU texture → sign — flattened to "},{"id":"spn-30695","marks":["bold"],"text":"960×653 at `scale 1.0000`"},{"id":"spn-30696","text":", prompt legible. §13 spent its whole length searching the environment and the cause was not in the environment: the official addon build "},{"id":"spn-30697","marks":["bold"],"text":"compiles its own GStreamer at branch 1.20"},{"id":"spn-30698","text":" and this machine runs "},{"id":"spn-30699","marks":["bold"],"text":"1.28.6"},{"id":"spn-30700","text":", so the shipped "},{"id":"spn-30701","marks":["code"],"text":"libproxy-encoding.so"},{"id":"spn-30702","text":" linked a GStreamer GL that was not the installed one. Every symbol resolved the entire time it was silently emitting nothing — "},{"id":"spn-30703","marks":["code"],"text":"ldd"},{"id":"spn-30704","text":" resolving is not evidence a native module matches its dependencies. The rebuild is now "},{"id":"spn-30705","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run addons"},{"id":"spn-30706","text":", pinned and hash-checked (§19)."}]},{"id":"blk-26423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30707","text":"Still true, and not smoothed over:"}]},{"id":"blk-26424","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30708","marks":["bold"],"text":"Frames tear — two thirds fixed, and the rest now measured"},{"id":"spn-30709","text":" (§20). It was"}]}],"id":"blk-26425","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30710","text":"never a damage-region problem. three left a "},{"id":"spn-30711","marks":["bold"],"text":"vertex array bound"},{"id":"spn-30712","text":" and Greenfield's YUV→RGB pass binds none of its own, so it recorded its attribute pointers into three's VAO and drew with three's leftovers; that was the full-canvas magnified-glyph artifact, and it is gone. Separately the decoded texture is "},{"id":"spn-30713","marks":["bold"],"text":"larger than the surface"},{"id":"spn-30714","text":" — 1024×770 for a 960×653 xterm — and the sign was mapping the padding too; it now samples the same sub-rect Greenfield's own shader does. What remains is a constant-slope diagonal with flat cyan below it, inside the decoded content: chroma left at default, so never written. That is upstream in "},{"id":"spn-30715","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-30716","text":", and the encoder A/B that would narrow it could not be run — see §20.3."}]},{"id":"blk-26428","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30717","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-window encode cost is still unpriced, and §21.2 says why."},{"id":"spn-30718","text":" Two"}]}],"id":"blk-26429","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26431","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30719","text":"harnesses, neither monotonic in window count. What they did establish: the proxy is flat at ~0.4% CPU while the browser sits at 425%, so the expensive half is decode and composite, not encode — \"per-window encode cost\" may be the wrong first question."}]},{"id":"blk-26432","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30720","marks":["bold"],"text":"Native launches drop above two"},{"id":"spn-30721","text":" (§21.3). Ask for four windows, get two,"}]}],"id":"blk-26433","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26435","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30722","text":"with nothing reported. Found while measuring something else, not diagnosed. The multi-window case is not just unpriced, it is unreliable."}]},{"id":"blk-26436","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26438","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30723","marks":["bold"],"text":"Signs carry no titles yet."}]}],"id":"blk-26437","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30724","text":"Closed since: a "},{"id":"spn-30725","marks":["bold"],"text":"reload no longer strands the remote client"},{"id":"spn-30726","text":" (§21.1) — each page load takes a fresh session id and "},{"id":"spn-30727","marks":["code"],"text":"pagehide"},{"id":"spn-30728","text":" reaps the old one, verified across three reloads against a proxy that was never restarted, leaving exactly one "},{"id":"spn-30729","marks":["code"],"text":"xterm"},{"id":"spn-30730","text":" behind."}]},{"id":"blk-26440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30731","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"},{"id":"spn-30732","text":" is no longer on this list — §16 closed it, and found on the way that a popup cannot map at all in Greenfield rc1."}]},{"id":"blk-26441","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30733","text":"Local patches — do not lose these"}]},{"id":"blk-26442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30734","text":"RRABBIT carries a "},{"id":"spn-30735","marks":["bold"],"text":"required"},{"id":"spn-30736","text":" one-line fix to "},{"id":"spn-30737","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-30738","text":": without it an "},{"id":"spn-30739","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"},{"id":"spn-30740","text":" can never map, so "},{"id":"spn-30741","marks":["bold"],"text":"no client can show a menu, dropdown or tooltip"},{"id":"spn-30742","text":". "},{"id":"spn-30743","marks":["code"],"text":"node_modules/"},{"id":"spn-30744","text":" is gitignored, so the fix lives in "},{"id":"spn-30745","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"patches/"}],"text":"`patches/`"},{"id":"spn-30746","text":" and is re-applied by "},{"id":"spn-30747","marks":["code"],"text":"postinstall"},{"id":"spn-30748","text":" and by "},{"id":"spn-30749","marks":["code"],"text":"build"},{"id":"spn-30750","text":". A runtime detector warns if it is ever missing rather than silently repairing it."}]},{"id":"blk-26443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30751","text":"Read "},{"id":"spn-30752","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"patches/README.md"}],"text":"`patches/README.md`"},{"id":"spn-30753","text":" before touching "},{"id":"spn-30754","marks":["code"],"text":"package.json"},{"id":"spn-30755","text":" scripts or upgrading "},{"id":"spn-30756","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-30757","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26444","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30758","text":"Lineage"}]},{"id":"blk-26445","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30759","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../RAVIO"}],"text":"RAVIO"},{"id":"spn-30760","text":" — the world this forks, and the source of every measured"}]}],"id":"blk-26446","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30761","text":"constant ("},{"id":"spn-30762","marks":["code"],"text":"S"},{"id":"spn-30763","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30764","marks":["code"],"text":"BOOST_X"},{"id":"spn-30765","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30766","marks":["code"],"text":"MIR_TILT"},{"id":"spn-30767","text":", the hood clip, the yoke camera framing)"}]},{"id":"blk-26449","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26451","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30768","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/PARKVPS"}],"text":"PARKVPS"},{"id":"spn-30769","text":" — the fleet whose rail proved"}]}],"id":"blk-26450","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26452","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30770","text":"the tab strip shape, and the origin of the "},{"id":"spn-30771","marks":["code"],"text":"Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Esc"},{"id":"spn-30772","text":" escape hatch"}]},{"id":"blk-26453","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30773","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/udevbe/greenfield"}],"text":"Greenfield"},{"id":"spn-30774","text":" — the in-browser Wayland"}]}],"id":"blk-26454","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26456","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30775","text":"compositor, AGPL-3.0"}]},{"id":"blk-26457","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30776","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://www.collabora.com/news-and-blog/news-and-events/wxrd-a-standalone-wayland-compositor-for-xrdesktop.html"}],"text":"wxrd"}]}],"id":"blk-26458","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26460","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30777","text":"/ "},{"id":"spn-30778","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/evil0sheep/motorcar"}],"text":"motorcar"},{"id":"spn-30779","text":" — the 3D-windowing prior art, and where the scoping decision comes from"}]},{"id":"blk-26461","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30780","text":"Licence"}]},{"id":"blk-26462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30781","text":"AGPL-3.0, inherited from Greenfield. See spec §9."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierag7cpawe2b73p66e324pydvtld3bdjscst2x6ynpkvahajxuijiea","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}